RULING ON THE RED GATE: SATISFIED, on P-013's terms and on no others. What the
remedy delivers is a reproducibility guarantee — any reader can check out 015a44f and
watch these exact assertions fail — and that is the whole of what the Patron ordered
in place of the waiver. What it does not and cannot restore is chronology: the
assertions for behaviours 7-9 were authored and green before the skeleton existed, and
09.log's fourth failure (:565) is the empty-needs-you case that the round-1 fix itself
added, so that particular red postdates the fix it guards. I say so plainly rather
than let the artifact imply otherwise. The Patron chose reproducibility over
chronology with the sequence already in the open; the artifacts now match the choice.

One residue, reproduced and unchanged from round 1: behaviour 7's negative case passes
against the skeleton (1 passed, board.spec.ts:244). An all-negative assertion is
