file outside *Files owned* and the round-1 disclosure list was touched
(w025.css was disclosed in round 1; route.ts, Inbox.tsx, harness.ts and
playwright.serve.config.ts are all unmodified).

Nothing blocking. Four residues, each stated with whether it is one instance or a class:

R1 — `everLoaded` is the right signal and the comment explaining why is accurate:
     boardModel always emits needs_you, so `columns.length === 0` never held, and
     officina/opera land from independently-resolving fetches, so
     `lifecycle.id !== ""` would have been the same bug one level up. I checked the
     initial load path: there is no separate loadAll — the first fetch is
     fullReconcile from the SSE's onOpen (reconcileReason "connect",
     Board.tsx:116-121), so everLoaded flips there and nowhere earlier. Correct,
     and transport-dependent by design (behaviour 7's negative case).
     `overflow-anchor: none` on .board__columns is scoped to this screen's own
     class and carries its measurement in the comment. No finding.

R2 — ADVISORY, one instance: fullReconcile's dispatch is a chain of three string
     equalities with `return fetchDrawerEvents(selectedId!)` as the else branch
     (Board.tsx:89-95). A fifth target added to reconcileTargets would silently be
     fetched as drawer events, and the `!` would be reached with selectedId
     undefined. It cannot happen today — behaviour 3 pins the list to exactly
     three-or-four — so this is a latent shape, not a bug. I checked: Board.tsx is
     the only consumer of reconcileTargets outside its own test (grep across
     apps/ and packages/), so one instance, not a class. Cheapest close would be
     a default that throws.

R3 — ADVISORY, one instance: the negative case now takes 13.5s of a 30s Playwright
     timeout (measured, `npm run -s test:serve`). 16s of headroom is fine today,
     but the 11s wait is the brief's floor, not a ceiling, and anything added to
     that case will run into the config's timeout rather than into a clear
     assertion. I checked every other case in board.spec.ts: the next slowest are
     the two reconnect cases at 4.6s and 4.7s, everything else is 1.1-1.7s. One
     instance.

R4 — ADVISORY, one instance, and I verified the builder's stated reason rather
     than taking it: B7's link targets `#/inbox`, the screen, not the petitio's own
     thread. There is no per-petitio deep link to target — apps/web/src/lib/route.ts
     maps four bare paths with no parameters, and Inbox.tsx selects a petitio only
     through local `focusIndex` state with no route or query input. Both files are
     outside *Files owned*, so building one here would have been the larger
     trespass. This satisfies *Patron rulings* ("links to the Inbox's existing
     answer flow") and stops a little short of behaviour 6's "links to its thread";
     the remainder belongs with W-073, where Reply itself lands. Accepted.

R5 — NOT a finding, recorded so the number is accounted: studio's advisory count
     119 -> 120 is the round-1 review gate's own uncertified evidence on
     studio/opera/W-064.md. No rule source changed (packages/cli/src/check.ts and
     rules/ have no diff in this round).

Carried forward from round 1, unchanged and not chargeable to the builder:

D6 — the *Acceptance* section asks the censor to drive a real browser by hand. I ran
     the scripted equivalent again (section 3) and it is honest evidence of
