5. VERDICT
=============================================================================

PASS, round 2. All eight blocking findings of round 1 are fixed, and each is fixed at
the root rather than at the symptom: every one now has an assertion that fails when
the defect is put back, proven by my own mutation, not by the builder's report. The two
live bugs are dead on the real officina where they were found, measured against round
1's own verbatim numbers. B8's seam is genuinely wired — the mutation that broke one
behaviour in round 1 now breaks two.

The red gate passes on P-013's recorded answer and on nothing else: the waiver stands
refused, D-024 is not extended, and the remedy the Patron named is satisfied by
re-execution I performed myself — checkout 015a44f, run the three named commands, watch
the same twelve assertions fail at the same spec lines, with the logs' tree hash
independently recomputed to be5cf928 and the condemned dirty:c032fb5b logs left intact
at 608b05b in an unrewritten history. P-012 stays open; behaviour 7's negative case
still passes against a skeleton, which is why it does.

No blocking findings. Four advisories (R2, R3, R4, and D6's three unattended items for
the Patron), none of which is a class.

